    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present to the market Apartment, 94 Bushy Park House. A superb second-floor, B-rated apartment positioned within this exceptionally well-maintained and highly sought-after development overlooking both the manicured internal gardens and the mature greenery of Bushy Park. \r\n\r\nEnjoying a prized west-facing aspect, this bright and spacious two-bedroom home benefits from excellent natural light throughout with its private balcony providing an ideal outdoor extension of the main living space and a perfect vantage point for afternoon and evening sun. The property’s elevated position combined with its peaceful internal setting offers a rare sense of privacy in such a central and established location.\r\n\r\nInternally, the accommodation is generous and well-balanced, extending to include two double bedrooms (main ensuite), a large open-plan living/dining space, separate kitchen and excellent storage throughout. The B-rated energy efficiency will lower running costs and greater long-term efficiency. \r\n\r\nThe development itself is immaculately maintained, set and surrounded by manicured grounds, mature trees that seamlessly connect to Bushy Park and offers designated and visitor parking.\r\n\r\nThe location of Bushy Park House remains one of the development’s greatest strengths. Positioned directly beside Bushy Park and within walking distance of both Terenure Village and Templeogue Village, residents benefit from immediate access to a wide range of cafés, restaurants, shops, supermarkets and amenities. The area is exceptionally well served by some of South Dublin’s most respected schools including Terenure College, Our Lady's School, St Pius X National School and Presentation."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway \r\nCeiling coving, intercom system, cloakroom off. \r\n\r\nLiving / Dining \r\nCeiling coving, gas fire with limestone fireplace, CH boiler off, double doors to kitchen and double doors to balcony. \r\n\r\nKitchen \r\nWide range of kitchen units, sink unit, extractor plumbed for dishwasher and washing machine and tiled floor. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (Ensuite )\r\nBuilt in wardrobes and double door to juliette balcony \r\nEnsuite \r\nBath with shower attachment, w.c, whb, tiled floor and part tiled walls. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\nBuilt in wardrobes\r\n\r\nOutside \r\nWest facing balcony off the living area, Juliette balcony off bedroom 1. Well maintained grounds within the development, designated and visitor parking."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "c. 78 sq. m. (839 sq. ft.)\r\nGFCH\r\nB3 – BER rating\r\nDesignated underground parking space\r\nManagement fees: c. €2,996 per annum\r\nYear of construction: 2001\r\nGenerously proportioned\r\nLift \r\nGreat transport links in the area. \r\nSecurity/ intercom system\r\nWithin easy reach of the villages of Terenure, Rathgar & Templeogue Villages\r\nEasy access to M50 and city centre"
      },
      {
